{"track":"tahsili","num":"4.01","title":"Trigonometry","sections":[{"heading":"Right-triangle trigonometric ratios","questions":[{"q":"In a right triangle, angle $\\theta$ has an opposite side of $5$ and hypotenuse $13$. Find $\\sin\\theta$ and the length of the adjacent side.","figure":{"type":"triangle","vertices":[[0,0],[12,0],[12,5]],"labels":[null,null,null],"side_labels":["adjacent","5","13"],"right_angle_at":1,"angle_marks":[{"vertex":0,"label":"θ"}],"width":200},"answer":"Adjacent $=\\sqrt{13^2-5^2}=\\sqrt{169-25}=\\sqrt{144}=12$. $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{5}{13}$."},{"q":"In a right triangle, angle $\\theta$ has an opposite side of $15$ and hypotenuse $17$. Find $\\cos\\theta$.","answer":"Adjacent $=\\sqrt{17^2-15^2}=\\sqrt{289-225}=\\sqrt{64}=8$. $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{8}{17}$."},{"q":"In a right triangle, angle $\\theta$ has an adjacent side of $7$ and hypotenuse $25$. Find $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\tan\\theta$.","answer":"Opposite $=\\sqrt{25^2-7^2}=\\sqrt{625-49}=\\sqrt{576}=24$. $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{24}{25}$, $\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{24}{7}$."},{"q":"In a right triangle, the two legs are $20$ and $21$, and the hypotenuse is $29$. Find $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$ for the angle $\\theta$ opposite the side of length $20$.","answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{20}{29}$, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{21}{29}$."}]},{"heading":"Special angles","questions":[{"q":"State the exact value of $\\sin(30^\\circ)$.","answer":"$\\sin(30^\\circ)=\\dfrac{1}{2}$."},{"q":"State the exact value of $\\cos(45^\\circ)$.","answer":"$\\cos(45^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$."},{"q":"State the exact value of $\\tan(60^\\circ)$.","answer":"$\\tan(60^\\circ)=\\sqrt{3}$."},{"q":"State the exact values of $\\sin(90^\\circ)$ and $\\cos(0^\\circ)$.","answer":"$\\sin(90^\\circ)=1$ and $\\cos(0^\\circ)=1$."}]},{"heading":"Converting between radians and degrees","questions":[{"q":"Convert $180^\\circ$ to radians.","answer":"$180^\\circ=\\pi$ radians."},{"q":"Convert $90^\\circ$ to radians.","answer":"$90^\\circ=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ radians."},{"q":"Convert $\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$ radians to degrees.","answer":"$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\times\\dfrac{180^\\circ}{\\pi}=150^\\circ$."},{"q":"Convert $270^\\circ$ to radians.","answer":"$270^\\circ=\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$ radians."}]},{"heading":"The Pythagorean identity","questions":[{"q":"Given $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{3}{5}$ with $\\theta$ acute, find $\\cos\\theta$ using $\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1$.","answer":"$\\cos^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{9}{25}=\\dfrac{16}{25}$. Since $\\theta$ is acute, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{4}{5}$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{5}{13}$ with $\\theta$ acute, find $\\sin\\theta$.","answer":"$\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{25}{169}=\\dfrac{144}{169}$. Since $\\theta$ is acute, $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{12}{13}$."},{"q":"Given $\\sin\\theta=0.6$, find $\\cos^2\\theta$.","answer":"$\\cos^2\\theta=1-0.36=0.64$."}]},{"heading":"Simplifying trigonometric expressions","questions":[{"q":"Simplify $\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta+1$.","answer":"$\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1$, so the expression equals $1+1=2$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\dfrac{1-\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$ (for $\\sin\\theta\\neq0$).","answer":"$1-\\cos^2\\theta=\\sin^2\\theta$, so the expression equals $\\dfrac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}=\\sin\\theta$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\tan\\theta\\cos\\theta$ (for $\\cos\\theta\\neq0$).","answer":"$\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$, so $\\tan\\theta\\cos\\theta=\\sin\\theta$."}]},{"heading":"Graphs: amplitude and period","questions":[{"q":"State the amplitude and period of $y=5\\sin(x)$.","answer":"Amplitude: $5$. Period: $2\\pi$."},{"q":"State the amplitude and period of $y=3\\cos(2x)$.","answer":"Amplitude: $3$. Period: $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}=\\pi$."},{"q":"State the amplitude and period of $y=2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{3}\\right)$.","answer":"Amplitude: $2$. Period: $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{1/3}=6\\pi$."},{"q":"A sine graph has amplitude $4$ and period $\\pi$. Write its equation in the form $y=A\\sin(Bx)$.","answer":"$A=4$. $B=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{\\pi}=2$. So $y=4\\sin(2x)$."}]},{"heading":"Graphs: phase shift and vertical shift","questions":[{"q":"The graph of $y=\\sin(x)$ is shifted $\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ to the right and $2$ units up. Write the new equation.","answer":"$y=\\sin\\left(x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)+2$."},{"q":"State the vertical shift and midline of $y=3\\cos(x)+5$.","answer":"Vertical shift: up $5$. Midline: $y=5$."},{"q":"The graph of $y=\\cos(x)$ is shifted $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ to the left. Write the new equation.","answer":"$y=\\cos\\left(x+\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$."}]},{"heading":"Solving basic trigonometric equations","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2\\sin\\theta=1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}$. Solutions: $\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=150^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta=1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","answer":"$\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Solutions: $\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=315^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=-1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","answer":"Solutions: $\\theta=135^\\circ$ or $\\theta=315^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $2\\cos\\theta+1=0$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","answer":"$\\cos\\theta=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$. Solutions: $\\theta=120^\\circ$ or $\\theta=240^\\circ$."}]},{"heading":"Reference angles in other quadrants","questions":[{"q":"Find $\\sin(150^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","answer":"The reference angle is $30^\\circ$; in Quadrant II, sine is positive. $\\sin(150^\\circ)=\\sin(30^\\circ)=\\dfrac{1}{2}$."},{"q":"Find $\\cos(240^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","answer":"The reference angle is $60^\\circ$; in Quadrant III, cosine is negative. $\\cos(240^\\circ)=-\\cos(60^\\circ)=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$."},{"q":"Find $\\tan(300^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","answer":"The reference angle is $60^\\circ$; in Quadrant IV, tangent is negative. $\\tan(300^\\circ)=-\\tan(60^\\circ)=-\\sqrt{3}$."}]},{"heading":"Complementary angle relationships","questions":[{"q":"Given $\\sin(20^\\circ)\\approx0.342$, use the relationship $\\sin\\theta=\\cos(90^\\circ-\\theta)$ to find $\\cos(70^\\circ)$.","answer":"$\\cos(70^\\circ)=\\sin(20^\\circ)\\approx0.342$."},{"q":"Given $\\sin(35^\\circ)\\approx0.574$, find $\\cos(55^\\circ)$.","answer":"$\\cos(55^\\circ)=\\sin(35^\\circ)\\approx0.574$."}]},{"heading":"The unit circle: coordinates of key points","questions":[{"q":"State the coordinates $(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)$ of the point on the unit circle at $\\theta=60^\\circ$.","answer":"$\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2},\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$."},{"q":"State the coordinates of the point on the unit circle at $\\theta=180^\\circ$.","answer":"$(-1,0)$."},{"q":"State the coordinates of the point on the unit circle at $\\theta=270^\\circ$.","answer":"$(0,-1)$."}]},{"heading":"Word problems: angles of elevation","questions":[{"q":"This question has two parts. A drone hovers directly above a landmark. From a point $200$ meters from the base of the landmark, the angle of elevation to the drone is $35^\\circ$.","parts":["Write an equation relating the drone's height $h$ to the given information, using the tangent ratio.","Find $h$, to the nearest meter, given $\\tan(35^\\circ)\\approx0.700$."],"answers":["$\\tan(35^\\circ)=\\dfrac{h}{200}$, so $h=200\\tan(35^\\circ)$.","$h\\approx200(0.700)=140$ meters."]},{"q":"This question has two parts. A ladder $10$ meters long leans against a wall, making an angle of $65^\\circ$ with the ground.","parts":["Write an equation for the height $h$ the ladder reaches up the wall, using the sine ratio.","Find $h$, to the nearest tenth of a meter, given $\\sin(65^\\circ)\\approx0.906$."],"answers":["$\\sin(65^\\circ)=\\dfrac{h}{10}$, so $h=10\\sin(65^\\circ)$.","$h\\approx10(0.906)=9.1$ meters."]}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Right-triangle trigonometric ratios","questions":[{"q":"In the right triangle shown, angle $\\theta$ has opposite side $8$ and hypotenuse $17$. Find $\\sin\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{17}{8}$","$\\dfrac{8}{15}$","$\\dfrac{15}{17}$","$\\dfrac{8}{17}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\dfrac{8}{17}$.","figure":{"type":"triangle","vertices":[[0,0],[15,0],[15,8]],"right_angle_at":1,"side_labels":["15","8","17"]}},{"q":"In a right triangle, angle $\\theta$ has opposite side $9$ and hypotenuse $41$. Find $\\cos\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{9}{41}$","$\\dfrac{9}{40}$","$\\dfrac{41}{40}$","$\\dfrac{40}{41}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Adjacent $=\\sqrt{41^2-9^2}=40$; $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{40}{41}$."},{"q":"In a right triangle, angle $\\theta$ has adjacent side $20$ and hypotenuse $29$. Find $\\sin\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{21}{20}$","$\\dfrac{20}{29}$","$\\dfrac{21}{29}$","$\\dfrac{29}{21}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"Opposite $=\\sqrt{29^2-20^2}=21$; $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{21}{29}$."},{"q":"In the right triangle shown, the two legs are $9$ and $40$, and the hypotenuse is $41$. Find $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$ (where $\\theta$ is opposite the side of length $9$).","choices":["$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{9}{40}$, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{40}{9}$","$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{40}{41}$, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{9}{41}$","$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{41}{9}$, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{41}{40}$","$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{9}{41}$, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{40}{41}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Opposite $=9$, adjacent $=40$, hypotenuse $=41$.","figure":{"type":"triangle","vertices":[[0,0],[40,0],[40,9]],"right_angle_at":1,"side_labels":["40","9","41"]}},{"q":"In a right triangle, angle $\\theta$ has opposite side $7$ and adjacent side $24$. Find $\\tan\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{24}{7}$","$\\dfrac{24}{25}$","$\\dfrac{7}{25}$","$\\dfrac{7}{24}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\dfrac{7}{24}$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Special angles","questions":[{"q":"State the exact value of $\\cos(30^\\circ)$.","choices":["$1$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\cos(30^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."},{"q":"State the exact value of $\\sin(45^\\circ)$.","choices":["$1$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\sin(45^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$."},{"q":"State the exact value of $\\tan(30^\\circ)$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$\\sqrt{3}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\tan(30^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sin(30^\\circ)}{\\cos(30^\\circ)}=\\dfrac{1/2}{\\sqrt{3}/2}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$."},{"q":"State the exact values of $\\cos(90^\\circ)$ and $\\sin(0^\\circ)$.","choices":["$\\cos(90^\\circ)=0$, $\\sin(0^\\circ)=1$","$\\cos(90^\\circ)=1$, $\\sin(0^\\circ)=0$","Both equal $1$","Both equal $0$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos(90^\\circ)=0$ and $\\sin(0^\\circ)=0$."},{"q":"State the exact value of $\\tan(45^\\circ)$.","choices":["Undefined","$\\sqrt{2}$","$1$","$0$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\tan(45^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sin(45^\\circ)}{\\cos(45^\\circ)}=1$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Converting between radians and degrees","questions":[{"q":"Convert $360^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$4\\pi$","$\\pi$","$2\\pi$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$360\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=2\\pi$."},{"q":"Convert $45^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$45\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$."},{"q":"Convert $\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$ radians to degrees.","choices":["$120^\\circ$","$150^\\circ$","$135^\\circ$","$270^\\circ$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}\\times\\dfrac{180}{\\pi}=135^\\circ$."},{"q":"Convert $210^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$","$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$210\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — The Pythagorean identity","questions":[{"q":"Given $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{4}{5}$ with $\\theta$ acute, find $\\cos\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{3}{5}$","$\\dfrac{4}{5}$","$\\dfrac{5}{3}$","$\\dfrac{9}{25}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\cos^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{16}{25}=\\dfrac{9}{25}\\Rightarrow\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{3}{5}$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{7}{25}$ with $\\theta$ acute, find $\\sin\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{576}{625}$","$\\dfrac{24}{25}$","$\\dfrac{25}{24}$","$\\dfrac{7}{25}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{49}{625}=\\dfrac{576}{625}\\Rightarrow\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{24}{25}$."},{"q":"Given $\\sin\\theta=0.8$, find $\\cos^2\\theta$.","choices":["$0.2$","$0.64$","$0.36$","$0.8$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\cos^2\\theta=1-0.8^2=1-0.64=0.36$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{12}{13}$ with $\\theta$ acute, find $\\sin\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{5}{13}$","$\\dfrac{13}{5}$","$\\dfrac{12}{13}$","$\\dfrac{25}{169}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{144}{169}=\\dfrac{25}{169}\\Rightarrow\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{5}{13}$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Simplifying trigonometric expressions","questions":[{"q":"Simplify $\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta-1$.","choices":["$2\\sin^2\\theta$","$0$","$2$","$1$"],"correct":1,"answer":"By the Pythagorean identity, $\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1$, so this is $0$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\dfrac{1-\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ (for $\\cos\\theta\\neq0$).","choices":["$\\dfrac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$","$\\cos\\theta$","$1-\\cos\\theta$","$\\sin\\theta$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$1-\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos^2\\theta$, so $\\dfrac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\cos\\theta$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\tan\\theta}$ (for $\\tan\\theta\\neq0$).","choices":["$1$","$\\sin\\theta$","$\\cos\\theta$","$\\dfrac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$, so $\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sin\\theta/\\cos\\theta}=\\cos\\theta$."},{"q":"Simplify $2\\sin^2\\theta+2\\cos^2\\theta$.","choices":["$1$","$0$","$2$","$4\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$2(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)=2(1)=2$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Graphs: amplitude and period","questions":[{"q":"State the amplitude and period of $y=4\\sin(x)$.","choices":["Amplitude $2\\pi$, period $4$","Amplitude $4$, period $2\\pi$","Amplitude $1$, period $4$","Amplitude $4$, period $\\pi$"],"correct":1,"answer":"For $y=A\\sin(Bx)$ with $B=1$: amplitude $=4$, period $=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{1}=2\\pi$."},{"q":"State the amplitude and period of $y=2\\cos(3x)$.","choices":["Amplitude $2$, period $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$","Amplitude $3$, period $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}$","Amplitude $6$, period $2\\pi$","Amplitude $2$, period $6\\pi$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Amplitude $=2$; period $=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$."},{"q":"State the amplitude and period of $y=5\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)$.","choices":["Amplitude $5$, period $\\pi$","Amplitude $5$, period $4\\pi$","Amplitude $\\dfrac{5}{2}$, period $2\\pi$","Amplitude $2$, period $4\\pi$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$B=\\dfrac{1}{2}$: period $=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{1/2}=4\\pi$; amplitude $=5$."},{"q":"A cosine graph has amplitude $3$ and period $4\\pi$. Write its equation in the form $y=A\\cos(Bx)$.","choices":["$y=3\\cos(4\\pi x)$","$y=4\\pi\\cos(3x)$","$y=3\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)$","$y=3\\cos(2x)$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$B=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{\\text{period}}=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{4\\pi}=\\dfrac{1}{2}$."},{"q":"The graph shows $y=A\\sin(x)$ for some $A$. Find $A$ by reading the graph's amplitude.","choices":["$A=1$","$A=2\\pi$","$A=4$","$A=2$"],"correct":3,"answer":"The curve's peak height (amplitude) is $2$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["2*sin(x)"],"xmin":-0.5,"xmax":6.5,"ymin":-3,"ymax":3}}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Graphs: phase shift and vertical shift","questions":[{"q":"The graph of $y=\\cos(x)$ is shifted $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ to the right and 3 units up. Write the new equation.","choices":["$y=\\cos(x)+\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}+3$","$y=\\cos\\left(x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+3$","$y=\\cos\\left(x+\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)+3$","$y=\\cos\\left(x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)-3$"],"correct":1,"answer":"Right shift: replace $x$ with $x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$; up $3$: add $3$."},{"q":"State the vertical shift and midline of $y=2\\sin(x)-4$.","choices":["Down 4, midline $y=2$","Up 4, midline $y=4$","Down 4, midline $y=-4$","Down 2, midline $y=-4$"],"correct":2,"answer":"Subtracting $4$ shifts down $4$; the midline is $y=-4$."},{"q":"The graph of $y=\\sin(x)$ is shifted $\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ to the left. Write the new equation.","choices":["$y=\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}-x\\right)$","$y=\\sin(x)+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$","$y=\\sin\\left(x+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$","$y=\\sin\\left(x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$"],"correct":2,"answer":"Left shift: replace $x$ with $x+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$."},{"q":"The graph shows $y=\\sin(x)$ shifted vertically. Find the new midline by reading the graph.","choices":["$y=0$","$y=2$","$y=1$","$y=-2$"],"correct":1,"answer":"The curve oscillates evenly about $y=2$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["sin(x)+2"],"xmin":-0.5,"xmax":6.5,"ymin":0,"ymax":4}}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Solving basic trigonometric equations","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\theta=45^\\circ$ only","$\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=135^\\circ$","$\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=225^\\circ$","$\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=120^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$: $\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $135^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sqrt{3}\\tan\\theta=3$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=300^\\circ$","$\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=210^\\circ$","$\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=240^\\circ$","$\\theta=60^\\circ$ only"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt{3}$: $\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $240^\\circ$ (tangent positive in Q1 and Q3)."},{"q":"Solve $2\\cos\\theta=1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=330^\\circ$","$\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=240^\\circ$","$\\theta=60^\\circ$ only","$\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=300^\\circ$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos\\theta=0.5$: $\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $300^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=225^\\circ$","$\\theta=45^\\circ$ only","$\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=315^\\circ$","$\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=135^\\circ$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Tangent is positive in Q1 and Q3: $\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $225^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $2\\sin\\theta+1=0$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\theta=210^\\circ$ or $\\theta=300^\\circ$","$\\theta=150^\\circ$ or $\\theta=330^\\circ$","$\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=150^\\circ$","$\\theta=210^\\circ$ or $\\theta=330^\\circ$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=-0.5$: $\\theta=210^\\circ$ or $330^\\circ$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Reference angles in other quadrants","questions":[{"q":"Find $\\sin(120^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","choices":["$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}$","$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Reference angle $60^\\circ$; sine is positive in Q2: $\\sin(120^\\circ)=\\sin(60^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."},{"q":"Find $\\cos(210^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Reference angle $30^\\circ$; cosine is negative in Q3: $\\cos(210^\\circ)=-\\cos(30^\\circ)=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."},{"q":"Find $\\tan(330^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","$\\sqrt{3}$","$-\\sqrt{3}$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Reference angle $30^\\circ$; tangent is negative in Q4: $\\tan(330^\\circ)=-\\tan(30^\\circ)=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$."},{"q":"Find $\\sin(315^\\circ)$ using the reference angle.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$","$-\\dfrac{1}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$","$\\dfrac{1}{2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Reference angle $45^\\circ$; sine is negative in Q4: $\\sin(315^\\circ)=-\\sin(45^\\circ)=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Complementary angle relationships","questions":[{"q":"Given $\\sin(25^\\circ)\\approx0.423$, use the relationship $\\sin\\theta=\\cos(90^\\circ-\\theta)$ to find $\\cos(65^\\circ)$.","choices":["$-0.423$","$0.906$","$0.577$","$0.423$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos(65^\\circ)=\\cos(90^\\circ-25^\\circ)=\\sin(25^\\circ)\\approx0.423$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos(40^\\circ)\\approx0.766$, find $\\sin(50^\\circ)$.","choices":["$0.643$","$0.766$","$1.306$","$0.234$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin(50^\\circ)=\\sin(90^\\circ-40^\\circ)=\\cos(40^\\circ)\\approx0.766$."},{"q":"Given $\\sin(70^\\circ)\\approx0.940$, find $\\cos(20^\\circ)$.","choices":["$1.064$","$0.060$","$0.342$","$0.940$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos(20^\\circ)=\\cos(90^\\circ-70^\\circ)=\\sin(70^\\circ)\\approx0.940$."}]},{"heading":"MCQ — The unit circle: coordinates of key points","questions":[{"q":"State the coordinates $(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)$ of the point on the unit circle at $\\theta=30^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2},\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$","$\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$","$(1,0)$","$\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos(30^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, $\\sin(30^\\circ)=\\dfrac{1}{2}$."},{"q":"State the coordinates of the point on the unit circle at $\\theta=90^\\circ$.","choices":["$(1,0)$","$(0,-1)$","$(0,1)$","$(-1,0)$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\cos(90^\\circ)=0$, $\\sin(90^\\circ)=1$."},{"q":"State the coordinates of the point on the unit circle at $\\theta=225^\\circ$.","choices":["$\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$","$\\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$","$(-1,-1)$","$\\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$225^\\circ$ is in Q3, reference angle $45^\\circ$: both coordinates negative, $-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$."},{"q":"The unit circle shown marks a point at angle $\\theta=60^\\circ$. What are its coordinates?","choices":["$\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},0.5\\right)$","$\\left(0.5,0.5\\right)$","$(1,0)$","$\\left(0.5,\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos(60^\\circ)=0.5$, $\\sin(60^\\circ)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.","figure":{"type":"circle","radius":1,"points":[{"angle":60,"label":"θ"}]}}]},{"heading":"MCQ — Word problems: angles of elevation","questions":[{"q":"A drone hovers directly above a landmark. From a point 150 meters from the landmark's base, the angle of elevation to the drone is $40^\\circ$. Find the drone's height, to the nearest meter.","choices":["$150$","$196$","$126$","$115$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$h=150\\tan(40^\\circ)\\approx126$ m."},{"q":"A ladder leans against a wall, making an angle of $70^\\circ$ with the ground. If the ladder shown is 12 meters long, find how high up the wall it reaches, to the nearest meter.","choices":["$4$","$12$","$8$","$11$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$h=12\\sin(70^\\circ)\\approx11$ m.","figure":{"type":"triangle","vertices":[[0,0],[10,0],[0,5]],"right_angle_at":0,"side_labels":[null,"12",null],"angle_marks":[{"vertex":1,"label":"70°"}]}},{"q":"From the top of an 80 m cliff, the angle of depression to a boat is $25^\\circ$. Find the horizontal distance from the base of the cliff to the boat, to the nearest meter.","choices":["$37$","$80$","$172$","$189$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\tan(25^\\circ)=\\dfrac{80}{d}\\Rightarrow d=\\dfrac{80}{\\tan(25^\\circ)}\\approx172$ m."}]}]}